": 18, "text": "C5 lost 12.5 points, taking Black's lead from +8.6 to +21.1. The engine wanted E2 instead. Black was well ahead after this, and the game was close only because of what followed."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "The 20k's B5 lost 12.0 points and turned a +9.6 lead into -2.4, with the engine preferring E6. Black's stones at B5 and B6 were then pressed against White's group at C5 and D5, and White briefly led."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "B7 was the worst move of the game, losing 17.7 points and moving the lead from -7.8 to Black +9.9. The engine wanted E6, the gap in Black's sixth-row wall. Black filled it next move, and the final board shows that wall running from A6 to F6."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script worked on the current position or on records. The stored `inspect` function and `current-position-liberties.js` parse the board and list chains and liberties, and for one move the player had already named it also reports the resulting chain and any captures. The other scripts replayed the finished game to check it, and wrote the SGF, game record and notes. None looped over empty points to score them or played a sequence forward.", "stop": false}}